The declared length `_read_bounded`
  compares is the file part's, so a file of exactly 50 MB is read (A19 rule
  4's required test);

a file over the size limit is refused before any of it is
parsed — a declared length over it before any byte is read, otherwise as
soon as more than it has been read;
